         Matrix res = new Matrix(n);\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n                    long tmp = 0;\n                    for (int k = 0; k < n; k++) {\n                        tmp += (long)a[i][k] * other.a[k][j];\n                    }\n                    res.a[i][j] = (int)(tmp % MOD);\n                }\n            }\n            return res;\n        }\n        \n        static Matrix clone(Matrix src) {\n            Matrix dst = new Matrix(src.n);\n            for (int i = 0; i < src.n; i++) {\n                System.arraycopy(src.a[i], 0, dst.a[i], 0, src.n);\n            }\n            return dst;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        int k = sc.nextInt();\n        sc.close();\n        \n        if (n == 0) {\n            // ans is identity, only a[k][k] = 1 (0-indexed column index k)\n            int res = 1 % MOD;\n            System.out.println(res);\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        // extract base-k digits, LSB first\n        ArrayList<Integer> digits = new ArrayList<>();\n        long tn = n;\n        while (tn > 0) {\n            digits.add((int)(tn % k));\n            tn /= k;\n        }\n        int cnt = digits.size();\n        \n        // allocate matrices\n        Matrix[][] f = new Matrix[cnt][k];\n        Matrix[][] sump = new Matrix[cnt][k];\n        Matrix[][] sums = new Matrix[cnt][k];\n        \n        // level 0\n        for (int j = 0; j < k; j++) {\n            f[0][j] = new Matrix(k+1);\n            f[0][j].setIdentity();\n            // set all columns of row j to 1\n            for (int col = 0; col <= k; col++) {\n                f[0][j].a[j][col] = 1;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // prefix sums for level 0\n        sump[0][0] = Matrix.clone(f[0][0]);\n        for (int j = 1; j < k; j++) {\n            sump[0][j] = f[0][j].multiply(sump[0][j-1]);\n        }\n        sums[0][k-1] = Matrix.clone(f[0][k-1]);\n        for (int j = k-2; j >= 0; j--) {\n            sums[0][j] = sums[0][j+1].multiply(f[0][j]);\n        }\n        \n        // build higher levels\n        for (int i = 1; i < cnt; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < k; j++) {\n                if (j == 0) {\n                    f[i][j] = Matrix.clone(sums[i-1][j]);\n                } else {\n                    f[i][j] = sump[i-1][j-1].multiply(sums[i-1][j]);\n                }\n            }\n            // prefix for this level\n            sump[i][0] = Matrix.clone(f[i][0]);\n            for (int j = 1; j < k; j++) {\n                sump[i][j] = f[i][j].multiply(sump[i][j-1]);\n            }\n            sums[i][k-1] = Matrix.clone(f[i][k-1]);\n            for (int j = k-2; j >= 0; j--) {\n                sums[i][j] = sums[i][j+1].multiply(f[i][j]);\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // process digits from most significant to least\n        Matrix ans = new Matrix(k+1);\n        ans.setIdentity();\n        int sum = 0;\n        for (int p = cnt-1; p >= 0; p--) {\n            int d = digits.get(p);\n            for (int j = 0; j < d; j++) {\n                int idx = (sum + j) % k;\n                ans = f[p][idx].multiply(ans);\n            }\n            sum = (sum + d) % k;\n        }\n        \n        // final result: sum of last column (index k) for all rows\n        long res = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i <= k; i++) {  // rows 0 to k inclusive (size = k+1)\n            res = (res + ans.a[i][k]) % MOD;\n        }\n        System.out.println(res);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.98\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00139639584813267, -0.030828183516860008, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0002889215829782188, -0.0007596705690957606, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00014482879487331957, -0.564511239528656, -0.0017178792040795088, -2.622600959512056e-06, 0.0, -2.13